# AMD64 thunk export spec -- uiautomationcore.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-17 corpus pass.  Boltgun imports this module STATICALLY and
# it had no guest thunk, so the loader refused the native ppc64 module
# (c000007b) and the whole image failed to load (c0000135).  Measured: the
# exe's import table names UiaRaiseAutomationEvent (ordinal 90),
# UiaRaiseAutomationPropertyChangedEvent (91), UiaClientsAreListening (58),
# UiaReturnRawElementProvider (98) and UiaHostProviderFromHwnd (76) -- the
# accessibility surface Slate registers whether or not a screen reader is
# running.
DLL uiautomationcore.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# Neither header is in the oracle's default translation unit, and
# uiautomationcoreapi.h does not compile on its own: it names PROPERTYID,
# which is typedef'd in the widl-generated uiautomationcore.h.  So that one is
# appended FIRST -- PROBE-EXTRA lines are emitted in the order written.
# Without them 35 of 37 exports were refused; with them, 34 of 37 are emitted,
# including four of Boltgun's five.
#
# The fifth is refused for a REAL reason and not an oracle gap:
# UiaRaiseAutomationPropertyChangedEvent takes two VARIANTs BY VALUE, and a
# VARIANT is 16 bytes -- wider than one 64-bit slot, which is the one shape
# this descriptor cannot express.  It keeps ordinal 91 as a named sentinel, so
# a guest that calls it faults by name rather than silently on half an
# argument.  (DllRegisterServer/DllUnregisterServer are the other two, and no
# Wine header declares them.)
PROBE-EXTRA   uiautomationcore.h
PROBE-EXTRA   uiautomationcoreapi.h
